      </characteristics>
    </profile>
  </sharedProfiles>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="The Black Rage" id="2893-070a-392e-4bc8" hidden="false">
      <description>All Blood Angel models gain +1 Strength and +1 Initiative in the turn in which they charge into close combat, or make a sweeping advance into an enemy unit. A Blood Angels unit that breaks or wipes out an enemy in hand-to-hand combat must advance if it could normally do so.
Additionally, at the start of every Blood Angels turn, roll a D6 for each Blood Angels unit in the army (including vehicles and independent characters). On a roll of 1, the unit moves D6&quot; forwards towards the enemy. This move does not affect the unit&apos;s movement in the movement or assault phase, but does mean the unit counts as moving for the purposes of using ranged weapons.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="The Death Company" id="e3ed-6222-7ab6-1f07" hidden="false">
      <description>For each unit of Honour Guard; Terminator Squad; Terminator Assault Squad; Veteran Squad; Tactical Squad; Scout Squad; Assault Squad; Veteran Assault Squad; Bike Squadron; Scout Bike Squadron; and Devastator Squad, toll a D6 at the start of the battle. On a 4 or 5 one model from the squad joins the Death Company. On a 6 one model joins the Death Company and you must roll again for the unit. Keep rolling unitl no more 6&apos;s have been rolled.
If you roll a 4+ for a squad let by a Veteran Sergeant, he may also join the Death Company.
The models that join the Death Company replace their equipment with the equipment listed in the Death Company roster.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Quickening" id="0cad-264f-40eb-f70b" hidden="false">
      <description>The Librarian may attempt to use the Quickening at the start of any assault phase. If successfully, one model in his unit gains +D3 Attacks in that phase.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
